Subject: shove: search for arc obstacles too
Upstream-file: pcbnew/router/pns_shove.cpp (SHOVE::shoveIteration)
Why: shoveIteration looks for the nearest obstacle by kind, in the order
 SOLID, VIA, SEGMENT, HOLE. ARC_T is in none of those masks, so an arc track
 is never found as an obstacle: a shove route goes straight through an arc of
 another net and the proposal violates clearance (tests/run_tests.py
 t_arc_obstacle_shove; the synthetic "arc" board). The iteration already has
 its ARC_T cases (onCollidingArc, the reverse-collision branch); only the
 search misses them. Arcs are searched together with segments, as the line
 they belong to is.
Upstream: yes - the same line is in KiCad master (2026-10-05); not yet proposed.

--- a/pcbnew/router/pns_shove.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/router/pns_shove.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
